  "title": "Then vs Now: daily rasters",
  "description": "Daily grids of noaacrwsstDaily analysed_sst (NOAA Coral Reef Watch CoralTemp 5 km SST, the product PacIOOS re-serves as dhw_5km/CRW_SST) around each sanctuary, one cloud-optimized GeoTIFF per place and year: 366 bands, band i = day-of-year i of a leap-year calendar, so a month-day is the same band in every year (band 60 = 29 Feb is NaN in non-leap years). Float32, nodata NaN, INTERLEAVE=BAND, 256 px tiles, DEFLATE with the floating-point predictor, EPSG:4326, 0.05 deg cells; every grid fits one tile, so reading one day for one place is one HTTP range request of a few kB. Converted from the archive of the NOAA ONMS climate-dashboard-app (extractr::ed_extract over a 20 %-buffered bounding box per sanctuary) by catalog/build_then_now.py. Read a band with geotiff.js; average the same band across year files for a custom 'Then'.",
  "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
